     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks too high and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**.\n- The maximum prescription daily dose is **3200 mg/day**.\n\nThis order would double both limits. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis looks like it could be a mix-up between a total daily dose and a per-dose amount. Did you mean one of these?\n1. **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day total)\n2. **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n3. **1600 mg four times daily as written.** If so, please confirm and give the reason, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you approved the dose above the maximum.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
